{
  "$comment": "Shared twin case table for the openapi family specifications §9.1: which JSON request-body\ndeclarations select WHOLE carriage (body.whole — an explicitly dynamic object or a\ndeclaration-complex JSON body) and which stay FLATTENED into named body properties.\nByte-identical copies live in openapi-client/go/testdata,\nopenapi-client/typescript/src/testdata, openbindings-go/formats/openapi/testdata and\nopenbindings-ts/packages/openapi/src/testdata.\n\nEach cell pins ONE (edition line × trigger keyword × presence) triple. The trigger\nkeywords are read under the GOVERNING EDITION'S dialect: on the 3.0 line the Schema\nObject is a defined subset whose own text makes unmentioned JSON Schema keywords\nstrictly unsupported, so patternProperties, if, then, else, dependentSchemas and\nunevaluatedProperties decide there as if absent; oneOf, anyOf, not and\nadditionalProperties are in both lines' dialects and decide alike on both. The\nunevaluatedProperties trigger is ANY-VALUE PRESENCE — the `false` spelling triggers\nexactly like `true` or a Schema Object.\n\nEvery harness renders the cell as a WHOLE OpenAPI document:\n  openapi: <openapi>; info {title: \"json body trigger scoping\", version: \"1\"};\n  servers [{url: <harness peer>}];\n  paths./items.post: operationId createItem, requestBody {required: true,\n    content: {\"application/json\": {schema: <schema>}}}, responses {\"204\": ...}.\n\nexpect is \"whole\" or \"flattened\", and each engine asserts it through its own\nSHIPPED path:\n  * The two openapi-client engines invoke twice. A FLAT input {\"value\": \"v\"}\n    dispatches {\"value\":\"v\"} when the cell is flattened, and refuses before\n    dispatch naming \"whole-value carriage\" when it is whole. A ROUTED one-tuple\n    whose body names {\"whole\": \"payload\"} with value.payload = {\"value\": \"v\"}\n    dispatches the same bytes when the cell is whole, and refuses naming\n    \"routed whole-body field does not identify any admissible whole-value\n    request-body candidate\" when it is flattened. Each harness supplies its own\n    envelope key and marker from its own profile constants.\n  * The two adapter engines synthesize. A whole cell publishes the one\n    protocol-neutral `payload` operation property and an inputTransform carrying\n    \"whole\":\"payload\"; a flattened cell publishes the artifact's own `value`\n    property and no `payload`.\n\nSpec: binding-specs/openapi/openbindings.openapi.md §9.1 (\"explicitly dynamic\",\n\"declaration-complex at the JSON body boundary\") at release/0.2. Census:\naudit/openapi-stage3-census.md items 2 and 3.",
